# Values

A value followed by `:name` defines it; `[name]` reads it anywhere.

Our budget is $3,000:budget and we've spent $2,444:spent.

remaining := budget - spent

We have [remaining] left, which is [remaining / budget] of the budget.

<!-- Brackets are optional when defining: $3,000:budget means the same and
is handy for text with spaces, as is "Oaxaca City":city. Write \: for a colon
that should not define anything. Try: change $2,444 and hover remaining. -->
